1. Subject to the rules noted hereunder and Nilgiris Fishing Rules, this licence covers fishing in all the waters under the
control of the Government of Tamil Nadu which have been specially reserved for trout fishing, except such as are
notified in paragraph 2 as closed for fishing, from time to time:-
Page 8/14

Nilgiris Fishing Rules, 1966
(a)
List of waters specially reserved for trout fishing,-
(i)
Mukurthi lake and river above Mukurthi lake;
(ii)
The Krurmund river above the falls (which is 200 meters below the confluence of Mekod river);
(iii)
The Partimund Stream and the Partimund Reservoir (when formed);
(iv)
The Mekod river below Mekod falls;
(v)
The reservoirs formed of the Avalanche and Emerald rivers including top waters;
(vi)
The Peerumund streams;
(vii)
Kokithurai stream;
(viii)
Chembar stream;
(ix)
Kalkundi stream;
(x)
The Upper Bhavani reservoir (when formed). Billithadahulla river with its tributaries (i.e.) Talakunda, Eakkidian
Deverbetta streams;
(xi)
The Bhavani puzha;
(xii)
Arokiampuzha and western catchment reservoir (when formed);
(xiii)
Parsons valley stream and the Parsons Valley Reservoir (when formed);
(xiv)
King Dhar stream and western catchment reservoir (when formed);
(xv)
Tirupanthorai stream;
(xvi)
Emeripuzha stream;
(xvii)
Silent valley stream;
(xviii)
Banghihullah stream and reservoir (when formed);
(xix)
Kaineerhundi; and
(b)
The holder of this licence can also fish for trout and carp in the following mixed fishing waters with any bait or line,
provided the total number of trout killed does not exceed the maximum catch of trout allowed in this trout licence:-
